# Industrial Brutalism & Tactical Telemetry UI

Architect interfaces synthesizing mid-century Swiss typography, industrial manufacturing manuals, and retro-futuristic aerospace/military terminals. Master rigid modular grids, extreme typographic scale contrast, purely utilitarian palettes, and programmatic analog degradation (halftones, scanlines, dithering). Project raw functionality and mechanical precision; deliberately discard consumer UI patterns.

## Pick one archetype and commit

Do not alternate or mix both within one interface.

**Swiss Industrial Print** — from 1960s corporate identity and machinery blueprints. High-contrast light mode (newsprint/off-white), monolithic heavy sans-serif, structural grids with visible dividing lines, asymmetric negative space punctuated by viewport-bleeding numerals, primary red as alert/accent.

**Tactical Telemetry / CRT Terminal** — from classified databases, mainframes, aerospace HUDs. Dark mode only, high-density tabular data, dominant monospace, technical framing (ASCII brackets, crosshairs), simulated hardware limits (phosphor glow, scanlines, low bit-depth).

## Typographic architecture

Typography is the primary structure; imagery is secondary.

**Macro (headers):** Neo-grotesque/heavy sans — Neue Haas Grotesk Black, Inter Black, Archivo Black, Monument Extended. Massive fluid scale (`clamp(4rem, 10vw, 15rem)`), tight negative tracking (`-0.03em` to `-0.06em`), compressed leading (`0.85`–`0.95`), uppercase only.

**Micro (data/telemetry):** Monospace — JetBrains Mono, IBM Plex Mono, Space Mono, VT323. Fixed small (`10–14px`), generous tracking (`0.05em`–`0.1em`), uppercase for all metadata, nav, unit IDs, coordinates.

**Textural disruption:** High-contrast serif (Playfair, EB Garamond) used exceedingly sparingly, heavily post-processed (halftone, 1-bit dither) to degrade vector perfection.

## Color system

Gradients, soft shadows, modern translucency are prohibited. Choose ONE substrate per project; never mix light and dark.

**Swiss Print (light):** bg `#F4F4F0`/`#EAE8E3` (matte paper), fg `#050505`–`#111111` (carbon ink), accent `#E61919`/`#FF2A2A` (hazard red — the only accent).

**Tactical (dark):** bg `#0A0A0A`/`#121212` (avoid pure black), fg `#EAEAEA` (white phosphor), accent same hazard red. Terminal green `#4AF626` optional, for a single element only — never general text.

## Layout & spatial engineering

Mathematically engineered, rejecting conventional padding. Strict CSS Grid — elements anchor to tracks/intersections, never float. Visible compartmentalization via solid `1–2px` borders; full-width `<hr>` to segregate units. Bimodal density: tightly packed monospace clusters against vast negative space framing macro-type. Absolute rejection of `border-radius` — all corners 90°.

## Components & symbology

ASCII framing: `[ DELIVERY SYSTEMS ]`, `< RE-IND >`, directionals `>>>` `///`. Industrial markers (`®` `©` `™`) as geometric structure, not legal text. Crosshairs (`+`) at grid intersections, barcode lines, warning stripes, randomized strings (`REV 2.6`, `UNIT / D-01`).

## Post-processing effects

**Halftone/1-bit dither** via SVG radial dot patterns + `mix-blend-mode: multiply`. **CRT scanlines** via `repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, transparent, transparent 2px, rgba(0,0,0,0.1) 2px, rgba(0,0,0,0.1) 4px)`. **Mechanical noise** — global low-opacity SVG grain on the DOM root.

## Engineering directives

1. `display: grid; gap: 1px;` with contrasting parent/child backgrounds for razor-thin dividers without border declarations.
2. Semantic rigidity — `<data>`, `<samp>`, `<kbd>`, `<output>`, `<dl>` to reflect telemetry's technical nature.
3. `clamp()` exclusively for macro-typography.

